        {
          "text": "The Map Room",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The map room occupies the quiet end of the neighborhood library. Its shelves hold folded street plans, ferry schedules, and hand-drawn routes collected over several decades. A small brass weight keeps each sheet flat while readers compare editions.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Mara volunteers on Thursday afternoons. She records the paper's date, the names of its surveyors, and any handwritten notes near the margins. When a street changes, she adds a transparent overlay rather than altering the older map.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Visitors often arrive looking for one address and leave with a longer story. They discover a footbridge that no longer exists, a lane named after a vanished orchard, or a public stair hidden behind a market. The archive cannot answer every question, but it can show where to ask next.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Keep a note of what the map cannot show.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "type": "quote"
    },
    {
      "lang": "text",
      "text": "copy → compare → annotate\n",
      "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A route index lives at ",
          "type": "text"
        },
